{{#extend "layout" showSource=true}}

  {{#content "main"}}
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Recipe &middot; output paths</p>
    <h1>Two sources, one path</h1>
    <p>
      The catalogue and the roasting bench both describe coffees, and both fan out into
      <code>shelf/</code>. One name appears in both. v1 wrote whichever page came last; v2
      fails the build naming the path, because only one of the two would ever exist on disk.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card">
      <h3>The catalogue owns its slugs</h3>
      <ul>
        {{#each model.catalogue}}
        <li><a href="shelf/{{slug}}.html">{{name}}</a> &mdash; {{origin}}</li>
        {{/each}}
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Bench lots, after the filter</h3>
      <ul>
        {{#each model.built}}
        <li><a href="shelf/{{slug}}.html">{{name}}</a> &mdash; {{origin}}</li>
        {{/each}}
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Dropped before registering</h3>
      <ul>
        {{#each model.dropped}}
        <li><code>{{slug}}</code> &mdash; {{note}}</li>
        {{/each}}
      </ul>
      <p class="meta tone-warn">Registered, this would have failed the build with <code>Page already processed: &hellip;/shelf/guji-uraga.html</code>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <pre><code>const claimed = new Set(catalogue.map((item) =&gt; utils.toSlug(item.name)))
const benchToBuild = benchLots.filter(
  (item) =&gt; !claimed.has(utils.toSlug(item.name)),
)</code></pre>
    <p>
      Four lines, and the priority is now written down rather than implied by registration
      order. That is the real gain: v1's behaviour depended on which <code>.pages()</code> call
      came last, which no reader of the script could see.
    </p>
  </div>
  {{/content}}

  {{#content "demo"}}
  <p>
    Both fan-outs share one view, <code>shelf/item.hbs</code>, and one controller file,
    <code>controllers/shelf-item.js</code>, which derives each slug with
    <code>utils.toSlug</code> — the same function the deduplication uses, so the Set and the
    output paths cannot disagree.
  </p>
  {{/content}}

{{/extend}}
